eOverlap\":1},{\"id\":94849,\"title\":\"When We Were Young\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zXRdw33nrtciNJspAeLcfE1QrVV.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2017,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.20923076923076925,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":96777,\"title\":\"The Silent Sea\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fFT0IgqtCOks4munDTxQwkvNJkd.jpg\",\"rating\":7.6,\"year\":2021,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.20476190476190478,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":211540,\"title\":\"Felix og Åmanden\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fSoBiBSJ9evy08LllqoZk3nJx7T.jpg\",\"rating\":10,\"year\":2022,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":10,\"seasonName\":\"Season 10\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/34NUX2XG9UDJAQg3sfIYSd6Dtzr.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2010-11-03\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"The Silver Pharaoh\",\"overview\":\"Tanis, Egypt, circa 1939. On the brink of World War II, an excavation team led by French archaeologist Pierre Montet unearthed an intact royal burial chamber containing treasures that rival the riches found in Tutankhamun’s tomb almost two decades before. But while the Tut discovery created an international sensation, the opening of the tomb in Tanis made barely a ripple in a world focused on impending war.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zw5axaOIsy1u9ANOUpz9qZg60UY.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-11-03\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Slave Ship Mutiny\",\"overview\":\"Three disparate Capetowners reveal a long-forgotten, dramatic slave ship revolt en route from Madagascar to South Africa. About half of Cape Town's population are descendants of White, Asian, and Black slaves captured by the Dutch East Indies Company from all around the Indian Ocean. After the captives force the surviving crew below deck, a brave Malagasy warrior and a devious Dutch company agent fight a battle of wits with many surprising turns. For some aboard, the journey ends on infamous Robben Island, where Tokyo Sexwale and Nelson Mandela were later imprisoned.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/kQ0kypPfxmfZlX8rd9nc7zbC4IS.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-11-10\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Lost Ships of Rome\",\"overview\":\"In 2009, archaeologists discovered an underwater graveyard of five Roman shipwrecks off the coast of Ventotene, a small Italian island with a notorious past. It was one of the biggest archaeological finds in recent history. The vessels’ well-preserved cargo indicates that these ships did not break up on the island’s rocks, but instead sank to the seabed intact and upright. They were laden with exotic goods including wine, olive oil, and the ancient delicacy garum; a condiment highly prized among ancient Romans. These sunken treasures are providing researchers with insight into the wreck, how the Romans lived, and Ventotene’s intriguing past.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dweoAnqxzlYtEluHFTPmyWotmjP.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-11-17\",\"runtime\":0}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2000-05-15\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}